- [P2] Compare optimized runtime hulls against rendered geometry — /Users/robin/.codex/worktrees/572c/Gold Rush/scripts/check-crawler-presentation.mjs:295-295
  `worldMorphBounds` reconstructs world coordinates from admission caches using the expected transform instead of checking the runtime callback’s points. An isolated CPU mutation restoring `mesh.matrixWorld` in the runtime hull loop leaves every parity assertion green, although the optimized hull differs from rendered geometry by 13–16 world units; raw geometry remains correct. Thus this seam can miss the production-only double-transform regression it should detect. Compare actual callback points against loaded mesh vertices transformed by their mesh world matrices in both morph states.
